<Project>

  <PropertyGroup>
    <!-- Avalonia.BuildServices arrives transitively with Avalonia and registers AvaloniaStatsTask,
         which runs BeforeTargets="CoreCompile" on every build. Its collector posts project name,
         target framework, runtime identifier, Avalonia version and output type to
         av-build-tel-api-v1.avaloniaui.net.

         Commandment 1: the agreed outbound surface is git.exe push/pull and nothing else. An
         outbound call that arrives through a dependency is the same decision taken sideways, so it
         is closed here rather than tolerated because nobody wrote the call.

         The task's only gate is UsedAvaloniaProducts, which Avalonia.props sets to ';AvaloniaUI'.
         Clearing it closes the condition, and unlike the AVALONIA_TELEMETRY_OPTOUT environment
         variable the task also honours, it stays true of a fresh clone and of CI.

         This has to be Directory.Build.targets, not .props: props is imported before the
         NuGet-generated imports, so Avalonia.props would simply set the property again afterwards.
         Verify with:  dotnet msbuild src\GrumpyGit.App -getProperty:UsedAvaloniaProducts  -->
    <UsedAvaloniaProducts></UsedAvaloniaProducts>
  </PropertyGroup>

</Project>
